A||||5||sqoach||85 and 86 gt noses: difference???||||5||
Z||000000||sqoach||12-20-2000||01:10 AM||||what's the difference between these two noses, or any aero type noses? besides the moulding of course. or is there a difference. they look the same to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-20-2000||01:12 AM||||Only difference is the molding.  Other than that all aero noses are the same.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-20-2000||01:42 AM||||The difference is that the molding being different and how the molding is mounted. On the 85 GT the molding is ribbed and is removable. On the 86-88 GT's it is smooth and part of the nose. It is not removable.<BR>The 84 Indy, 85 GT and 86/87 SE noses are the same.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-20-2000||08:11 AM||||Squoach,<P>Oreif has it backwards so far as the 'removeable' parts go. Only the marker lights are removeable on the '85 GT and SE's. Please just turn the statement around. Also, along with the '85 GT nose it applies as well to the '85 & '86 SE's as well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-20-2000||12:08 PM||||I love correcting somebody who is correcting someone else. The 85 SE nose IS NOT an aero nose, it's the pointy wedge nose...I know because I have one.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">   <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, etc...||||reg||1
